While the meat finishes frying, I set the table in the living room.
My dining area is quite small.
But there is plenty of room for Kasper, Sara, and me.
I take three plates out of the cupboard.
I place them on the small table.
Afterwards, I open the drawer with cutlery.
I take out forks and knives.
I lay a fork and a knife by each plate.
We will also need three glasses for water.
I fetch those out in the kitchen.
Finally, I take some light blue paper napkins from a package.
I fold them nicely.
Then I put a napkin on each plate.
Now the table is set and ready for guests.
I walk back to the stove.
The meatballs are still sizzling in the hot pan.
I take the pan off the heat.
I am completely ready to have guests.
